From: nell <nellkh2007@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 10:32:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] read the opponent's commit whichever way they spell Step-0

MOAAMOHA told us before playing that their Step-0 record is
record_type: "step_zero" and that their reader already accepts our
type: "system_spec" as equivalent. That sentence is the finding: they are
tolerant and we were not, so their report would have carried our commit while
ours carried "unknown" for theirs - a hole in exactly one of the two files an
auditor joins, discovered only after a counted series was filed.

Interop generosity has to be mutual, or the stricter side quietly produces the
poorer evidence and never notices, because its own artifacts look complete from
the inside.

Both scopes are searched as well as both spellings, since placement varies too;
payload wins on a collision because that is the half the commit-reveal digest
covers. Nothing is loosened: a record must still declare itself Step-0, so a
turn record carrying a github_commit cannot impersonate the declaration.
